{"key":"2e64dedd-0996-4cd6-b6cd-4f055a46c38c","installationKey":"9ec56080-ef8d-488a-af71-1e2de5ed7bbc","publishingOrganizationKey":"609765e0-4ce8-11db-b80e-b8a03c50a862","doi":"10.15468/ewxvjj","version":"101.168","external":false,"numConstituents":0,"type":"OCCURRENCE","title":"Amphibian Specimens","description":"<p>The Herpetology collection currently contains nearly 52,000 cataloged specimens of amphibians and reptiles. A large proportion of the collection is composed of amphibians and reptiles from the United States (46 states are represented), and many of these species are from the Southern Plains and Oklahoma. Approximately 60% (~31,000 specimens) of the collection is made up of Oklahoma specimens, making it the largest repository of Oklahoma amphibians. The collection also contains specimens from a total of 50 countries, with relatively large numbers from Brazil, Mexico, Ecuador, and Egypt. An early collection of specimens is from the Galapagos Islands of Ecuador.</p>","language":"eng","homepage":"http://samnoblemuseum.ou.edu/collections-and-research/herpetology/","logoUrl":"http://65.52.215.125/ipt/logo.do?r=amphibian","citation":{"text":"Siler C, King P (2019). Amphibian Specimens. Version 101.168. Sam Noble Oklahoma Museum of Natural History. Occurrence dataset https://doi.org/10.15468/ewxvjj accessed via GBIF.org on 2026-10-26.","citationProvidedBySource":false},"contactsCitation":[{"key":6920754,"abbreviatedName":"Siler C","firstName":"Cameron","lastName":"Siler","roles":["ORIGINATOR"],"userId":[]},{"key":6920755,"abbreviatedName":"King P","firstName":"Paul","lastName":"King","roles":["METADATA_AUTHOR"],"userId":[]}],"lockedForAutoUpdate":false,"createdBy":"609765e0-4ce8-11db-b80e-b8a03c50a862","modifiedBy":"crawler.gbif.org","created":"2014-03-06T22:18:06.961+00:00","modified":"2026-02-20T18:21:18.586+00:00","contacts":[{"key":6920754,"type":"ORIGINATOR","primary":true,"userId":[],"firstName":"Cameron","lastName":"Siler","position":["Curator"],"email":[